From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Meadlock <jmeadlock@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): rotate decode queries on a rank dealt no index
 rows

Base: vLLM 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus the candidate-62 series
(0001..0829, spark-ds41f-1120). vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/attention.py and the
test file are byte-identical under the candidate-69-r2 series (0001..0857), so
the same diff applies there; the hunks below were cut from that tree.

Rationale:
1. The overlapped decode path (0767) defers q's RoPE and the shared decode
   metadata to the aux stream and issues them from inside select_rows' loop
   over this rank's index chunks, beside the first _index_chunk.
2. _decode_index_split deals a decode step's index rows across the TP ranks
   (SPRows(rows, tp, rank): ceil(rows / tp) rows each, in rank order) once the
   step has 24 rows or more, or on an eager decode past 16,384 tokens.
3. When (tp - 1) * ceil(rows / tp) >= rows the last rank is dealt no rows.
   _index_query already returns empty queries for it, select() never reaches
   the chunk loop, and the deferred RoPE is never issued. forward_mqa then
   attends with un-rotated queries on that rank's heads, on every layer with
   an indexer, for every row of the step (rows at position 0 are unaffected:
   the rotation there is the identity).
4. The overlap needs rows <= DECODE_CHUNK (64), so with the 24-row threshold
   the last slice is empty at: TP8 25..28, 33..35, 41, 42, 49; TP7 24, 29, 30,
   36; TP6 25; TP2..TP5 never. Only TP8 is affected: on TP5..TP7 the trailing
   ranks own no attention heads after _trim_padded_groups (8 output groups do
   not divide), and _rope(q) is already skipped there. The eager long-context
   branch splits from rows >= tp, where smaller worlds would also have an empty
   last slice (TP3 at 4 rows, TP4 at 5, 6 and 9). It was not reached in the
   experiment: at TP4 with 20,000 tokens of context every decode step replayed a
   captured graph.
5. The deferred work moves into issue_pending_aux(), which runs once per
   forward: beside the first index chunk as before, or right after select()
   when this rank scored nothing. The existing wait_stream join is unchanged.

Quality:
Output-changing only on the affected steps, where it restores the arithmetic
the same rows get in a step of any other size. Every other step issues the
same kernels on the same streams in the same order. Measured in
experiments/2026-11-23-decode-rope-empty-index-slice.

Tests:
- tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py: the two-stream overlap test
  also runs a rank-split step where this rank is dealt no rows, and one where
  it is dealt two. Without the fix: 1 failed, 79 passed (no rope(q) on the
  empty slice). With it: 80 passed. (candidate-69-r2 image, one GB10.)

Upstream status: local DeepSeek V4.1 TileLang decode overlap; nothing to send
upstream.
---
diff --git a/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py b/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py
index 8019f38..0d9e4a2 100644
--- a/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py
+++ b/tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py
@@ -1901,6 +1901,40 @@ def test_decode_two_stream_overlap_schedules_disjoint_workspaces(monkeypatch):
     assert ("index_chunk", "main") in names_reidx
     assert ("attend", "main") in names_reidx
 
+    # A rank-split decode step (24 rows or more, or a long eager decode) deals the
+    # index rows across the ranks. The deferred rope(q) + decode metadata still run
+    # once per forward on a rank dealt none of them, which scores no index chunk:
+    # rank 2 of 4 rows on 3 ranks here, as the last rank of 25..28 rows on 8.
+    module.compressor = comp
+
+    class _FakeSplit:
+        local_rows = 2
+
+        def __init__(self, start, real_rows):
+            self.start, self.real_rows = start, real_rows
+
+        def gather(self, x):
+            return torch.zeros(4, 512, dtype=torch.int32)
+
+    for split in (_FakeSplit(4, 0), _FakeSplit(0, 2)):
+        events.clear()
+        for key in [k for k in vars(ctx) if k != "attn_metadata"]:
+            delattr(ctx, key)  # per-forward caches (index pages, decode metadata)
+        monkeypatch.setattr(
+            cls, "_decode_index_split", lambda self, *a, _split=split: _split
+        )
+        module._forward(
+            torch.arange(4, dtype=torch.int64),
+            torch.zeros(4, 32, dtype=torch.bfloat16),
+        )
+        real = split.real_rows
+        assert [e for e in events if e[:2] == ("rope", "q")] == [
+            ("rope", "q", "aux")
+        ], real
+        assert events.count(("decode_metadata", "aux")) == 1, real
+        assert events.count(("index_chunk", "main")) == (1 if real else 0), real
+        assert events[-1] == ("attend", "main"), real
+
 
 @pytest.mark.parametrize("is_decode", [False, True])
 @pytest.mark.parametrize("n_real", [4, 2, 0])
